          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## September Pending Close review\n\n- **Work order:** WO-2025-09-004 — **MO-25-09-1070** (Cooler Plate Pack, Racine)\n- **Source transaction:** TXN-ISSUE-250930-1070 (component issue; event CE-250904-0004)\n- **Amount:** **$318,250.75** (31,825,075 cents)\n- **Event created:** **2025-09-30T20:25:00**\n- **September period entered Pending Close:** **2025-09-30T18:00:00**\n- **Elapsed after Pending Close:** **145 minutes** (2 hours 25 minutes)\n- **Recorded accounting status:** **POSTED**\n- **Consistent with Oracle’s Pending Close treatment? No.** Oracle’s Cost Management 26B policy says transactions created after Pending Close are not processed, with specified exceptions such as revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments. This is a component INPUT event, not one of those exceptions, so POSTED is inconsistent with the documented treatment.\n\nThe review was read-only; no database records were changed.",
